    "turn_idx": 40,
    "turn_text": "we haven't heard in any of the debates so far has been any sort of conversation about housing or the homeless. What would you like to hear in this next campaign? The number one issue, the Public Policy Institute says that this is the number one issue in California, even up there with the economy, concerns about the economy. What do you want to hear the candidates talk about in the next Democratic debate about housing and homelessness? There are three things we can do. First, to have a housing first policy, meaning the best thing to do with people is not just to put them in some temporary housing, but it's to get them permanent housing and to help integrate them into society. We need to have first a increase in Section 8 vouchers. I mean, in my county, in Santa Clara County, you have a shortage of people who can qualify for Section 8 vouchers. Second, we need to have intervention when people are about to default on their rent so you can intervene before they default. And we have a very successful program in Santa Clara County that's funded by private resources to do that because once you get an eviction on your record, it becomes much harder to get back into housing. We should have a federal program that does that. And third, we need to expand dramatically the tax credit for affordable housing, and that tax credit is used by builders to build far more affordable housing so we can increase the supply. If we did those three things and invested billions of dollars at the federal level, we would go a long way to having affordable housing for people who are homeless.",
